{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qbmmrparqku7ochh4p5eqsqu62ujeie2eskbsgjqf6yff65jhv3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases complete, verified with my own commands. Summary:\n\n## What the library is\nThe entire C library in `c_src/` is **one function** — `char *tool_basename(char *path)` (returns the byte after the last `/` or `\\`). `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly **1** symbol. Nothing was left untranslated.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all created in the crate root)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 1 C export (`tool_basename`) → present in Rust `.so`; symbol diff empty; all Rust `U` symbols are libc/unwind |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 10 rows, derived by grepping the C: it has **no** error return/assert/range check, so the rejection surface is the unchecked contract violations (NULL, unterminated buffer, zero length, separator-as-last-byte, all-separators, oversized, high-bit bytes, post-NUL data, idempotence) + E10 documenting that no enum exists in the ABI |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 28 rows: no runtime options exist, so the axes are the 4 branch outcomes (`s1`/`s2` NULL-ness, `s1>s2`) × input shapes (length sweeps over 15/16/17/31/32/33/63/64/65/127/128/129, 1 MiB & 4 MiB, separator position/count/adjacency, 0x80–0xFF signed-char bytes, unaligned string starts 0..15, garbage after NUL, chained calls, exhaustive pairwise placements) |\n\nFeature combinations: `Cargo.toml` has **no** optional features and the C has no `#ifdef`/CMake options → exactly **one** combination. Both `dev` and `release` (`panic=abort`) Rust artifacts are tested anyway.\n\n## Phases B/C — differential tests\n`tests/{common/mod.rs,configs.rs,errors.rs}` load **both** `.so` files with `libloading` and call only exported symbols. 40 tests, ~150k randomized inputs (fixed-seed SplitMix64), comparing returned pointer offset, returned string bytes, and buffer non-mutation; NULL/unterminated-buffer rows fork a child and compare the **exact termination signal**.\n\n## Bug found and fixed (in the Rust, not the C)\n**E1 diverged for real:** the original translation re-implemented `strrchr` as a Rust byte loop, so `tool_basename(NULL)` hit rustc's debug null-deref assertion → `SIGABRT` + stderr message, while C faults with `SIGSEGV` silently. Fixed by calling the same libc `strrchr` the C source calls (`unsafe extern \"C\"` block) — now identical in both profiles, and the Rust `.so` imports `strrchr@GLIBC_2.2.5` just like the C one.\n\n## Phase D — completion gate\n- `./check_symbols.sh`: 0 missing, 0 undefined non-libc symbols (debug **and** release).\n- `./run_all.sh`: **rc=0** — 80 passing test results (40 × 2 artifacts), all 28 `CONFIGS.md` and all 10 `ERRORS.md` rows checked, under the single feature combination.\n- **Negative controls** prove the suite isn't vacuous: a `.so` ignoring `\\` fails 19/29 + 7/11 rows; a `.so` that null-checks instead of faulting fails `e1_null_pointer`.\n- Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the requested `build/` output)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":81737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":976,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"044e9b11-e627-4161-8667-18f16392eab7","uuid":"2743d562-a05e-4460-a19f-3bb73fa08cfc","timestamp":"2026-08-20T06:37:05.199Z"}
